      <tei:div type="colophon" subtype="introduction">
        <tei:p>This is a macaronic poem for Yom Meturgeman on the 8th of the month of Tevet. Macaronic poetry is poetry in multiple languages at once. In this case, the languages reflected are Hebrew, Aramaic, Judeo-Arabic, Yiddish, Ladino, and English, with a repeated Hebrew refrain. Each language is meant to rhyme with the colloquial Hebrew as it would be read — i.e. though the Yiddish doesn’t rhyme with the modern Hebrew pronunciation, it rhymes with the traditional Ashkenazi one.</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
      <j:endConditional target="#osp_53696_introduction"/>
